From 559845f317ef5933f3fadca1e21e538b81f48861 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 07:38:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 073/119] scene-referred S2: the physical preset, the probe
 convention, and the content documentation

Fifth and last item of Stage S2, and the only one that is mostly content. Items 1 to 4 make the
engine measure light honestly; this one ships the numbers a scene needs to be lit with, the
convention a probe has to carry, and the page that tells a user why their level changed.

Decision: scene-notes/decisions/s2-preset-and-probes.md, part 1 approach A and part 2 approach A.
Research: scene-notes/research/s2-tod-defaults-and-probe-bake.md.

PART 1 - ReC_Physical.env

- A new .env preset with its .cryasset sidecar, at
  Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/Assets/Environment/, alongside the ODT cubes the plugin already
  ships. NOT a code change: time-of-day defaults and ranges live in CTimeOfDayVariables::Reset(),
  which is shared construction-time code, and every existing .env stores its own min/max, so
  widening anything there would move the stock path and still not reach a single existing preset.
  Approach B (the camera writing values programmatically on activation) was rejected because it
  silently rewrites the artist's lighting; approach C (widening the code defaults) is the
  stock-path change this avoids. default.env is not touched - it is the template every new level
  in the engine is created from.

- Real photometric values: sun 100 000 lux at midday falling to 1 000 at 06:00/18:00 and 0 at
  night, skybox 20 000 lux with its range widened IN THE FILE from 20 000 to 200 000 (the stock
  default sat at 99 % of its own ceiling), night-sky horizon/zenith multipliers at 2e-6 / 1e-6
  where stock has 1e-4 / 2e-5 - about twenty times a real moonlit sky - the deprecated HDR dynamic
  power factor pinned at 0, the engine's EV window widened to -4..20 so it can never clamp while
  the camera owns exposure, and fog off (it is S8). Saved at preset version 3, the same version
  the shipped default.env uses, whose loader matches variables by id and ignores the rest - so the
  preset only carries what it changes.

- DOCUMENTED DEVIATION. The task asked for a preset that opens looking right at the camera's
  shipped Manual defaults AND for a sun of ~100 000 lux. Those are 6.2 stops apart and cannot both
  be true: T5.6, 1/50, ISO 400 is EV100 8.615 (L_sat 470 cd/m2), physical midday is EV100 14.8.
  The physical values were kept - D1 makes real light ratios the point, and the sun/shade
  acceptance test needs them - and the gap is closed the way it is closed on a set, with ND. The
  arithmetic is worked through in the docs: ND Filter 6 gives EV100 14.615, L_sat 30 100 cd/m2,
  and an 18 % sunlit surface at 0.203, within a quarter stop of 0.18. The alternative (scaling the
  curves down 64x) is offered and its cost stated - the panel stops meaning lux.

PART 2 - the probe convention

- The bake path adds a _rec suffix while the switch is on, in front of the _cm the texture system
  needs at the end, and re-points the probe entity at the file it actually wrote. A probe baked
  under the scene-referred convention is byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a stock one - the .dds has no
  version field and the RC has nowhere to put one - yet the two differ by up to 3.3 stops. The
  filename is the stamp until ReCS owns the RC (approach B, a DDS header field) or ships a sidecar
  (approach C); both are recorded and deferred.

- One CryWarning per probe at load when the file's stamp disagrees with the convention the frame
  is lit under, naming the probe and both conventions. A stale probe otherwise looks like a
  lighting mistake rather than a stale asset, which is precisely the pit D13 forbids leaving.

- Verified rather than assumed: the bake already renders at unity exposure. S1's latch forces the
  pre-exposure to 1.0 for SHDF_CUBEMAPGEN, so the cube map stores unexposed radiance and the
  runtime tint multiply exposes it exactly once. It inherits the PI convention from the
  engine-side switch, which is item 1's deliberate decision not to force that one to unity.

  THIS ADDS A FOURTH DLL: the probe bake and load are header-inline in
  CryDefaultEntities/DefaultComponents/Lights/EnvironmentProbeComponent.h, so CryDefaultEntities
  is rebuilt and has to be deployed. There is no renderer-side seam that can do it - the filename
  is decided by the component, and WriteTIFToDisk cannot rename it without stranding the RC call
  and the reload that follow.

PART 3 - documentation

- docs/SceneReferredContent.md: what changes and why (the per-source stops table: local lights
  -1.65, textured skybox -3.32, sun and ambient and emissive unchanged), installing and exposing
  the preset, the sun/shade ratio being a property of geometry and not of the preset, the probe
  re-bake procedure with its five gotchas, and a symptom/cause/fix table. It states plainly the
  three things a user will otherwise discover the hard way: area lights are not yet corrected and
  are 1.65 stops hot, the legacy .tod migration is path-dependent, and the procedural sky is
  uncalibrated.

- docs/ConsoleReference.md gains r_SceneReferredNishitaScale and the r_HDRDebug 1 skybox unit
  line; README.md points at both new documents from the Scene Referred property row and says in
  bold that a level looks different by design.

Built clean (0 errors, 0 warnings outside Code/SDKs): CryDefaultEntities, CinematicCamera.

